Babet 2.6.0 roadmap
====================

[x] Evaluate libarchive and define the multi-format archive API.
[x] Add secure TAR inspection and extraction.
[x] Add deterministic TAR creation.
[x] Add .tar.gz/.tgz, .tar.xz/.txz, .tar.bz2/.tbz2/.tbz and
    .tar.zst/.tar.zstd/.tzst support.
[x] Define the 2.6.0 boundary for standalone gzip/xz/bzip2/zstd streams:
    keep them outside the archive API until a dedicated raw-stream contract is
    designed.
[x] Complement std::regex in babet.find with a bounded safe glob mode.
[x] Replace the legacy regex implementation with locally built static RE2 and
    preserve the documented matching semantics.
[x] Introduce shared strict Lua validation helpers without changing public
    contracts.
[x] Evaluate archive creation from explicit file lists and exclusion rules:
    defer the feature until archive-root, collision and symlink semantics are
    specified by a concrete use case.
[x] Audit code, tests, FR/EN documentation, examples and PDF manuals before
    release, using the same standard as 2.5.0.

Deferred ideas retained in notes.md:
- standalone compressed streams with a dedicated raw-stream API;
- archive creation from explicit lists and exclusion rules;
- parent-side PATH resolution followed by execve;
- worker-to-worker channels;
- cooperative cancellation design;
- macOS/BSD portability.
